<form class="fso-obs-helper">
  <h2>OBS Setup — No Foundry Login</h2>
  <p><strong>Status:</strong> {{connected}}</p>
  <p>This overlay does not open Foundry inside OBS. Do not use OBS Interact and do not log a Foundry user into the Browser Source.</p>
  <ol>
    <li>In OBS, open <strong>Tools → WebSocket Server Settings</strong> and enable the WebSocket server.</li>
    <li>In Foundry module settings, enter the same OBS host, port, and WebSocket password.</li>
    <li>In OBS add <strong>Sources → + → Browser</strong>.</li>
    <li>Turn on <strong>Local file</strong> and browse to:<br><code>{{overlayPath}}</code></li>
    <li>Set Width to <strong>{{width}}</strong> and Height to <strong>{{height}}</strong>.</li>
    <li>Place your normal Foundry Window/Game Capture underneath this transparent Browser Source.</li>
  </ol>
  <p class="notes">The Browser Source contains only the GM/player HUD. Foundry sends LVL, AC, HP, and Death Saving Throws directly to OBS.</p>
  <div class="form-group">
    <button type="button" data-action="reconnect"><i class="fas fa-plug"></i> Reconnect to OBS</button>
    <button type="button" data-action="test"><i class="fas fa-vial"></i> Send Test Data</button>
  </div>
</form>